{
  "summary": "The app largely follows the design tokens and passes automated accessibility (axe) checks, but the core user journey is broken. After policy acceptance the Dashboard never reaches the EmptyState (\"No activity yet\") – the UI stays in a loading state and the acceptance flow does not navigate correctly. This prevents the primary flow (add receipt/mileage in two taps) from working and is a high‑severity defect. Several secondary issues also need fixing: missing landmark roles, incomplete accessibility labeling on tab icons and FABs, hard‑coded dimensions that ignore the desktop layout spec, and occasional use of ad‑hoc colors instead of the theme token palette. These issues reduce usability, keyboard navigation, and visual consistency, especially on web and larger screens.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Dashboard never exits the loading state when there are no receipts or mileage entries, so the EmptyState with the title \"No activity yet\" is never rendered. The UI flow test times out waiting for this copy.",
      "fix": "Ensure the data‑loading logic resolves (e.g., handling the empty SQLite result set) and sets a `loading` flag to false. When receipts and mileage arrays are empty, render the `EmptyState` component with the exact copy defined in DESIGN.md. Add a fallback `catch` to clear loading on DB errors and display the error message as specified."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "After checking the \"I agree\" box and tapping Continue, navigation to the Dashboard does not happen reliably (race condition with SecureStore write). The flow sometimes stays on the PolicyScreen, causing the Dashboard step to be unreachable.",
      "fix": "Make the Continue handler `async`, await `SecureStore.setItemAsync` (or the abstraction in `policy.ts`), then use `navigation.reset({ index: 0, routes: [{ name: 'Dashboard' }] })` to guarantee navigation. Also disable the button while persisting to avoid double taps."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabNavigator.tsx",
      "issue": "Icon‑only tab items lack explicit `accessibilityLabel`/`accessibilityHint`, so screen‑reader users cannot identify the target tab.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel={label}` and `accessibilityRole=\"tab\"` to each `BottomNavigation` route definition. Ensure the label matches the visible text (e.g., \"Dashboard\", \"Receipts\")."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The shared `Screen` wrapper does not declare a landmark role (`accessibilityRole=\"main\"`). This violates the accessibility hierarchy required in the spec.",
      "fix": "Wrap the root `View` in `<SafeAreaView accessibilityRole=\"main\" ...>` or add `accessibilityRole=\"main\"` to the outermost view. Verify that nested headers use `accessibilityRole=\"header\"` as the spec describes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "On web the button lacks a visible focus indicator (outline) when navigated via keyboard, which breaches the \"visible focus\" requirement.",
      "fix": "Add a CSS rule (or `style` prop) for `:focus-visible` that sets `outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary)` and increases contrast. React Native Paper already supports `rippleColor` but ensure the focus style is applied for non‑touch devices."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FAB.tsx",
      "issue": "The FAB is not keyboard focusable on web and does not have a visible focus outline, making it inaccessible for keyboard users.",
      "fix": "Set `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` and `tabIndex={0}` on the FAB, and add a `:focus-visible` outline style matching the design token (e.g., 2 px solid `var(--color-primary)`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen width is hard‑coded to `maxWidth: 420` regardless of viewport size, so the desktop specification (max‑width 560 px) is not met.",
      "fix": "Detect screen width via `useWindowDimensions()` or a media query and set `maxWidth: width >= 1280 ? 560 : 420`. Keep the 16 px padding from the theme spacing."
    },
    {
